{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a stitch task (#5680) for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires implementing three files in `pkg/format/` according to SRD srd003-format requirements R1, R2, R3:\n   - `pkg/format/humansize.go` — Implement HumanSize with binary (1024) and SI (1000) unit conversion\n   - `pkg/format/color.go` — Implement ANSI color output for file types with terminal detection\n   - `pkg/format/columns.go` — Implement PadRight, PadLeft, and Columns for tabular alignment\n   \n   This is an automated code generation task managed by the cobbler orchestrator. No git commands should be run. All code must compile and pass `go vet`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - SRD-driven implementation (srd003-format)\n   - GNU coreutils compatibility (ls -C column layout, ls default LS_COLORS)\n   - ANSI escape sequences for terminal colorization\n   - Terminal detection via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl (pkg/sys.IsTerminal)\n   - Human-readable size formatting (binary 1024-based vs SI 1000-based)\n   - Unicode display width via utf8.RuneCountInString (not byte count)\n   - Package-level state management for color override (SetColorEnabled/ResetColorEnabled)\n   - Differential testing pattern used throughout the project\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd003-format.yaml** (read for full requirements)\n     - Defines R1 (column alignment), R2 (ANSI color), R3 (human-readable size)\n     - R1.1: Columns distributes entries into max columns fitting termWidth, per-column width from longest entry\n     - R1.3: Use rune count for display width, not byte count\n     - R1.4: Entries go top-to-bottom then left-to-right (GNU ls -C behavior)\n     - R2.1-R2.7: FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n     - R2.3: ColorEnabled does type assertion to *os.File, calls sys.IsTerminal(f.Fd())\n     - R2.4: GNU ls default colors: dir=34(blue), symlink=36(cyan), exec=32(green), block=33;1, char=33;1, socket=35(magenta), pipe=33(yellow), regular=0\n     - R2.6: SetColorEnabled overrides auto-detection (process-global)\n     - R2.7: ResetColorEnabled reverts to auto-detection\n     - R3.1-R3.4: HumanSize with HumanSizeOpts{Binary bool}\n     - R3.2: Binary=true → base 1024, suffixes [\"\", \"K\", \"M\", \"G\", \"T\", \"P\", \"E\"]; Binary=false → base 1000, suffixes [\"\", \"kB\", \"MB\", \"GB\", \"TB\"]\n     - R3.3: One decimal place for non-integer values (e.g., 1536→\"1.5K\")\n     - R3.4: Return \"0\" for zero bytes\n\n   - **pkg/sys/terminal.go** (read for IsTerminal interface)\n     - Key dependency for ColorEnabled implementation\n     ```go\n     func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool {\n         _, err := unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)\n         return err == nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/format/pad.go** (read, essentially empty)\n     - Only contains copyright header and `package format`\n     - Not in the files-to-modify list, should not be touched\n\n   - **pkg/format/humansize.go** (stub to be modified)\n     ```go\n     type HumanSizeOpts struct {\n         Binary bool\n     }\n     func HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string {\n         panic(\"not implemented\")\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/format/color.go** (stub to be modified)\n     - Has stubs for FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled (all panic)\n\n   - **pkg/format/columns.go** (stub to be modified)\n     - Has stubs for PadRight, PadLeft, Columns (all panic)\n\n   - Existing test files listed: `pkg/format/color_test.go`, `pkg/format/humansize_test.go`, `pkg/format/pad_test.go` (contents not shown but exist)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD and pkg/sys/terminal.go to understand the IsTerminal interface and full requirements\n   - Identified that AC3 in the task description mentions \"1.0Ki\" but the SRD uses \"K\" suffix for binary mode — the SRD is the source of truth\n   - Noted the R2.3 pattern: type assert writer to *os.File, then call sys.IsTerminal(f.Fd())\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task description providing full project context, SRDs, source code stubs, execution constitution, go style constitution, task requirements, constraints, and acceptance criteria for implementing pkg/format (task #5680)\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Request for a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement `pkg/format/humansize.go` — HumanSize function with binary/SI conversion\n   - Implement `pkg/format/color.go` — FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n   - Implement `pkg/format/columns.go` — PadRight, PadLeft, Columns\n   - Verify: `go build ./pkg/format/...` succeeds\n   - Verify: `go vet ./pkg/format/...` reports no issues\n   - Verify all 5 acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three reference files (SRD, terminal.go, pad.go) and was about to begin implementing all three format package files. No code has been written yet. The implementation plan is:\n\n   **humansize.go**: Implement HumanSize — handle zero→\"0\", iterate through unit tiers dividing by base (1024 or 1000), format with `fmt.Sprintf(\"%.1f%s\", val, suffix)` for non-integers and `fmt.Sprintf(\"%d%s\", val, suffix)` for whole numbers.\n\n   **color.go**: Add package-level `colorOverride *bool` variable. FileTypeColor checks override/auto-detect, returns ANSI codes per R2.4. ColorEnabled does `*os.File` type assertion then `sys.IsTerminal(f.Fd())`. SetColorEnabled sets the override. ResetColorEnabled nils it.\n\n   **columns.go**: PadRight/PadLeft use `utf8.RuneCountInString` for display width. Columns tries decreasing column counts from max down to 1, computing per-column widths from longest entry in each column, distributing entries top-to-bottom then left-to-right.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write all three implementation files (humansize.go, color.go, columns.go) in full, then run `go build ./pkg/format/...` and `go vet ./pkg/format/...` to verify compilation. Per the task's implementation strategy: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands.\"\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement — Complete the work described in Requirements and Files to Create/Modify. Follow the Design Decisions.\"\n\n   Key design decisions to follow:\n   - D1: ColorEnabled uses pkg/sys.IsTerminal\n   - D2: SetColorEnabled stores override in package-level variable\n   - D3: HumanSize rounds to one decimal place, omits decimal for whole numbers\n   - D4: May import pkg/sys, must not import any cmd/ package\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5680/316401c8-9433-40c1-9339-2903c911b953.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"316401c8-9433-40c1-9339-2903c911b953","uuid":"23c8b2c3-a78f-41e8-b9ff-7a34fe927e16","timestamp":"2026-05-30T17:04:20.592Z","isSynthetic":true}
