{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Dy4YJ1vx21RQU9nRky1dUK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three files implemented, all tests pass, build and vet clean.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n- **`pkg/format/humansize.go`** — `HumanSize` converts byte counts to human-readable strings. Values < 10 with a unit suffix get one decimal place (`1.0K`, `1.5K`), values >= 10 use integer format (`10K`). Zero returns `\"0\"`. Binary mode uses base 1024 with `K/M/G/T/P/E` suffixes; SI mode uses base 1000 with `kB/MB/GB/TB`.\n\n- **`pkg/format/color.go`** — `FileTypeColor` returns GNU ls LS_COLORS default ANSI codes (bold blue for dirs, bold cyan for symlinks, etc.). `ColorEnabled` does `*os.File` type assertion then calls `sys.IsTerminal`. `SetColorEnabled`/`ResetColorEnabled` manage a process-global override via `*bool` pointer.\n\n- **`pkg/format/columns.go`** — `PadRight`/`PadLeft` use `utf8.RuneCountInString` for display width. `Columns` tries decreasing column counts, distributing entries top-to-bottom then left-to-right (GNU ls -C layout), with per-column widths from the longest entry in each column plus 2-space gaps."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":39820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"316401c8-9433-40c1-9339-2903c911b953","uuid":"86757755-9569-4ce4-bc62-d2a5e8344b25"}
